You have not been paying attention to which victims are peaceful and
which are hostile during your sacrifest.  Here's the relevant lines from
mon.c on what happens when you kill a monster:

	} else if (mtmp->mpeaceful)
		adjalign(-5);

Killing a peaceful costs 5 points of numerical alignment.  The number
has a maximum based on how far into the game you are but no minimum. 
The more peacefuls you kill the lower you can get.

First you killed a lot of peacefuls with the rubber chicken.  Then you
did sacs until you moved your numerical alignment to zero or small
positive.  Then you started seeing clovers.  Then you created and killed
a peaceful.  When you sacced the corpse of the peaceful it gained you
under 5 alignment points so your net ended up negative or zero.

Alignment points aren't earned by killing hostiles.  Alignment points
are earned by killing always-hostiles and cross-aligned hostiles.  It's
far from obvious in play but monsters come with their own deity
alignments and you get no points for killing a hostile of your own
deity alignment. If you're neutral and you kill a hostile neutral
there's no benefit except you survived the experience. If you're
neutral and you kill a chaotic there is a benefit. The trouble for a
neutral character in the mines is the mines are filled with neutral
alignment monsters.

It's hard for a neutral player to have a high alignment in the mines. 
It's easy for any character who kills a lot of peacefuls to have a low
numerical alignment.  It's very easy for a neutral who kills a lot of
peacefuls in the mines to have a negative alignment.

I try to count 3 hostiles killed after each time I kill a peaceful
before I will attack another peaceful.  For a neutral player that's not
enough in the mines.

A couple of years ago there was a really good write-up on this topic. 
It suggested that killing 2 jackals would cover killing a peaceful.

Killing peacefulls is worse:

	if((mtmp->mpeaceful && !rn2(2)) || mtmp->mtame)	change_luck(-1);

Sometimes it reduces your luck without telling you.   Players who kill a
lot of peacefuls need to use altars.


